{
  "summary": "The investigation focuses on whether a missing temporary instruction or an active change record contributed to the air loss event during un-released work preparation.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "statement": "Work boundary was not formally released/accepted by Maintenance receiver M-A at the time of the incident.",
      "type": "finding",
      "status": "verified","sourceIds":["structuredIncident.conditions[1]","IA-S02_work_package_cover.md · representative section"],"testNeeded":"None"}
    ],
  "questions":[
    {
      "intent":"Determine if a temporary instruction was required for the specific work scope (WO-527) and whether its absence constituted a procedural gap.",
      "text":"Does WO-527 require an attached Temporary Instruction per site policy, given that it involves maintenance of 1SC dryer group D-101 in the RHOB area?",
      "rationale":"The work package cover shows a blank temporary instruction field. Confirming whether this was required or optional determines if missing documentation is a causal factor.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["Site procedure for Temporary Instruction attachment requirements","Work history of WO-527 to see prior similar tasks"],"priority":"high",
      "sourceIds":[],
      "routedTo":[]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Verify if a Change Record (MOC) was active that altered service routing or pressure thresholds.",
      "text":"Was there an approved Management of Change record affecting the instrument air distribution to RHOB on May 20, 2024?",
      "rationale":"The structured incident lists 'Status of any change records' as unknown. An unrecorded MOC could explain why normal pressure bands or alarm thresholds were different.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["MOC register for May 20","Engineering disposition logs"],"priority":"high",
      "sourceIds":[],
      "routedTo":[]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Clarify the mechanism of air restoration to distinguish between automatic recovery and manual intervention.",
      "text":"Did the return to normal pressure at 10:07 AM result from an automated compressor restart sequence or a manual operator action?",
      "rationale":"Understanding if systems were self-healing versus requiring human input affects whether procedural gaps in monitoring contributed to the event duration.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["SCADA logs for RHOB service station","Compressor control logic diagrams"],"priority":"medium",
      "sourceIds":[],
      "routedTo":[]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Establish if alarm thresholds were altered or standard, which impacts the severity of the 'air-low' indication.",
      "text":"What was the numeric value of the low-pressure alarm threshold and normal band limits for RHOB header H-R on May 20?",
      "rationale":"The incident packet notes these values are unknown. If thresholds were lowered by a change record, the event might have been expected; if standard, it suggests an anomaly.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["Alarm configuration records","Historical trend data for H-R"],"priority":"medium",
      "sourceIds":[],
      "routedTo":[]
    }
  ],
  "handoffs":[

  ],"decision":{"summary":"The investigation has identified a critical procedural gap: work was underway without formal release. The next step is to determine if missing documentation (temporary instruction) or an unrecorded change record caused the vulnerability.",
      "evidenceUsed":["structuredIncident.conditions[1]","IA-S02_work_package_cover.md"],"unknowns":[

      ],"alternatives":["The air loss was a random distribution failure unrelated to work procedures.","A temporary instruction existed but was lost or not attached by error."],
